642	Scrotoschisis: Management Challenges and Review of Literature	Tunde Talib Sholadoye, Halima Oziohu Aliyu, Suleiman Baba, Philip Mari Mshelbwala, Emmanuel Adoyi Ameh	\N	2024-09-18		315	<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n          <jats:p>Scrotoschisis (extracorporeal testicular ectopia) is a rare congenital defect of the scrotal sac associated with the extrusion of one or both testicles. The exact mechanism causing the anomaly is largely unknown. This is a report of two infants aged 3 and 4 days, respectively, presented with infected unilateral extracorporeal testicular ectopia. Both infants had orchidopexy and repair of the scrotal defect following debridement of the infected defects and administration of broad-spectrum parenteral antibiotics. The infants have remained well at 3 years of follow-up. The isolated unilateral disease was described by several authors. Delayed presentation in scrotoschisis results in superimposed infection which complicates surgical management resulting in a prolonged hospital stay.</jats:p>	journal-article	0	10.4103/ajps.ajps_122_23	Medknow	No license URL	No publisher location	22	0189-6725	\N	\N	0974-5998		https://doi.org/10.4103/ajps.ajps_122_23	\N
