ho studied e-learning and face-to-face education, with (p=0.868 &gt; α). Ho is accepted, which means that the transition to e-learning rather than face-to-face education had no negative impact on academic achievement, it was found that nursing students academic achievement is not negatively affected by the Corona   pandemic. Conclusion: In this way, e-learning can be harnessed and developed to advance the nursing education agenda. Further study is recommended to assess the impact of e-learning on students’ academic achievement on other courses.</jats:p>	journal-article	0	10.54361/ljmr.17-17	Medical Research Center	https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0	No publisher location	0	2312-5365	179	172	2413-6069		https://doi.org/10.54361/ljmr.17-17	\N
