8332	Study the Effects of Mass in a Simple Damped Harmonic Motion of a Mass-spring System Using Simulation	 Ali. S. Al-Nuaimi,  Ola A. Mohammed	\N	2021-08-25		3996	<jats:p>The effect of mass on the behavior of oscillatory systems in a damped spring-mass system was studied using simulation. It was found that the mass affects the amplitude and displacement in the case of an undamped oscillatory system. In critically damped systems, the mass affects the displacement exponentially, and the system doesn’t oscillate. In the case of an overdamped system, there is also no oscillatory motion, and an increase in the mass was not affected, since the system gets to rest very quickly. The study shows that simulation can be a very helpful tool to study the behavior of oscillatory physical systems.\nKeywords: Simple harmonic motion damped mass-Spring system, simulation</jats:p>	journal-article	0	10.36811/ljbs.2021.110069	RAFT IT and Publications Pvt Limited	No license URL	No publisher location	0	2707-6261	88	81	2707-627X		https://doi.org/10.36811/ljbs.2021.110069	\N
