hey had only abdominal pain (4.2%). Significant risk factors associated with the occurrence of these parasitic infections include: lack of awareness, history of diarrhea, poor toilet hygiene, poor toilet-student ratio, as well as infrequent visits to the hospital for medical check-ups/laboratory tests. Conclusion: Giardia lamblia and Cryptosporidium parvum co-infection does .......</jats:p>	journal-article	1	10.36349/easjpid.2022.v04i02.001	SASPR Edu International Pvt. Ltd	No license URL	No publisher location	0	2663-0982	22	10	2663-6727		https://doi.org/10.36349/easjpid.2022.v04i02.001	\N
