2003	Afrotropical Bird Biology	nan	2790-0592	https://journals.uct.ac.za/index.php/ABB	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	nan	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	'Afrotropical Bird Biology' is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to advancing the understanding of birds inhabiting the Afrotropical region. Its scope encompasses a wide range of topics, including avian ecology, evolution, behavior, conservation, and taxonomy. The journal prioritizes original research papers, review articles, and short communications that contribute to a deeper understanding of the biology, diversity, and conservation of Afrotropical bird species. \r\n\r\nKey themes within 'Afrotropical Bird Biology' encompass a diverse array of topics, such as the impact of climate change on bird populations, habitat fragmentation and its effects on avian communities, the role of birds as ecosystem engineers, and the evolution of unique adaptations in Afrotropical birds.  The journal also provides a platform for research exploring avian diseases, the effectiveness of conservation strategies, and the use of new technologies in avian research. \r\n\r\nThe journal's audience comprises a broad range of professionals involved in avian research, including ornithologists, ecologists, conservation biologists, wildlife managers, and researchers from related disciplines. The journal serves as a vital resource for both established scientists and emerging researchers interested in the ecology and evolution of birds in the Afrotropical region. 'Afrotropical Bird Biology' facilitates the dissemination of cutting-edge research findings, fosters collaboration among researchers, and provides a platform for discussions on important conservation challenges facing Afrotropical birds.\r\n\r\nThe journal's impact extends beyond its publication of research findings. It plays a critical role in informing conservation efforts by highlighting the vulnerabilities of Afrotropical bird species, identifying conservation priorities, and advocating for 